<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soleyman Khan Ardalan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soleyman Khan Ardalan was a wali of Ardalan, the Kurdish principality on the Safavid frontier with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. In the 1630s he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanandaj">Sanandaj</a> (Sinneh) as the new capital of the Ardalan rulers, and the town remained the seat of the dynasty until its end in the nineteenth century.</p></div>
